 "text": "-->\nHome | recassnmo\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nBack to News\nBack to News\nBack to News\nRECORDERS' ASSOCIATION OF MISSOURI\nAbout\nCommittee Assignments\nResources\nFall Meeting Documents\n2021-2025 Conference Documents\nNotification Programs\nCalendar\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nWhat We Do\nLearn more about RAM and what recorders do.\nLearn More\nNOTIFICATION PROGRAMS\nLearn more about County Recorders' free notification programs to provide property owners an early warning in case of fraudulent activity.\nMore information\nLEGISLATION\nThe Recorders Association of Missouri monitors legislation proposed in Missouri's General Assembly for its impact on recording offices and the real estate industry.\nMore information\nRESOURCES\nRAM offers a listing of resources which can assist both Recorders and community members.\nMore information\nABOUT RAM\nOUR HISTORY\nThe Recorders’ Association of Missouri (RAM) was founded in 1984 in Kansas City, Missouri at the Annual Conference of the Circuit Clerks and Recorders Association.\nThe Recorders voted to establish an organization having the sole purpose of educating Recorders of Deeds in the State of Missouri on all aspects of recording law and procedures.\nCOUNTY-SPECIFIC INF0\nTHANK YOU CONFERENCE SPONSORS\n​ Platinum Sponsors - Fidlar Technologies, iCounty Technologies, and Revolution data systems\nAbout\nCommittee Assignments\nResources\nFall Meeting Documents\n2021-2025 Conference Documents\nNotification Programs\nCalendar\nMore\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\n© 2025 by The Recorders Association of Missouri\nbottom of page",
